title: $:/nikorion/language/en-GB/SourceOnly/

Title: ! Browser edits go to the source
Rule: ''You can edit the look from the web interface of this dev wiki'' (Theme tweaks, a stylesheet or a setting tiddler of the plugin): the change is written back into the plugin sources and the file is removed from `wiki/tiddlers/`.
Why: With `pnpm dev`, the dev server notices the file the browser just saved, finds the tiddler by title in `src/theme/` (a `.tid` file, or a line of `overrides/vanilla.multids`), updates it, then deletes the saved copy so the plugin's shadow tiddler takes over again. Nothing stays in the wiki.
Where: Written back: stylesheets (`src/theme/styles/`), overrides (`src/theme/overrides/`), Vanilla settings (a new one is appended to `vanilla.multids`). Left alone: tiddlers unknown to the plugin, multi-line values for `vanilla.multids`, and `$:/palette`, `$:/view`, `AnimationDuration` (never saved in this wiki).
